    "# Pandas — Session 1: Introduction, Series & DataFrames\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "NumPy gave us powerful numerical arrays. But real-world data is rarely just numbers in a grid — it has column names, row labels, mixed data types, and missing values. **Pandas** is built exactly for this kind of data.\n",
    "\n",
    "Pandas is the most widely used data analysis library in Python. It is built on top of NumPy, so everything you learned about NumPy carries forward — Pandas adds a richer, labelled structure on top.\n",
    "\n",
    "Pandas has two core data structures:\n",
    "\n",
    "| Structure | What it is | Equivalent to |\n",
    "|-----------|-----------|---------------|\n",
    "| `Series` | 1-dimensional labelled array | A single column of data |\n",
    "| `DataFrame` | 2-dimensional labelled table | A full spreadsheet or SQL table |\n"
   ]
