    "## Part 2: Pandas Series\n",
    "\n",
    "A **Series** is a one-dimensional array with an **index** — a label attached to each value. If you think of a dictionary, a Series is like a more powerful dictionary that supports arithmetic, statistics, and alignment.\n",
    "\n",
    "```\n",
    "Index    Value\n",
    "  0   →   88\n",
    "  1   →   76\n",
    "  2   →   91\n",
    "  3   →   55\n",
    "```\n",
    "\n",
    "The index does not have to be numbers — it can be strings (like student names), dates, or anything unique.\n",
    "\n",
